{
  "slug": "artist:astrix",
  "name": "Astrix",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Georgia and based in Tel Aviv, Avi Shmailov, known as Astrix, has been a major figure in the Israeli trance scene since 1997. His early studio work focused on the nitzhonot style, an offshoot of Goa trance that featured anthemic arrangements, as seen on the Ptzatzot 3 compilation featuring his tracks In Peace and Eakhis World. By 2002, he signed to the HOMmega Productions label and released his debut album, Eye to Eye. His sound is noted for solid, driving basslines and crisp, spacious acoustics, a trait highlighted by author Graham St John. In 2006, he gained global recognition by placing 41st in DJ Mag's Top 100 DJs list, climbing to 18th in 2007. Throughout his career, he has performed at international festivals including Dance Valley, Love Parade, and Creamfields. His discography includes studio albums such as 2004's Artcore, 2010's Red Means Distortion, and 2016's He.art, while his 2009 record One Step Ahead was the first from his catalog released on a USB flash drive.",
